  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating sanctions pressure raises counterparty and geopolitical tail‑risk premia, decreasing dealers' willingness to warehouse long‑dated Treasuries and widening bid‑ask spreads, which directly lowers secondary market depth and resiliency.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_iran_confrontation</data>
  <data key="d39">us_treasury_market_stres</data>
