<edge source="us_treasury_market_stres::short_term_funding_liqui" target="russia_ukraine_war::external_aid_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved short‑term funding liquidity (cheaper/available repo and interbank lines) directly reduces payment frictions and collateral constraints for banks and exporters, enabling faster letters of credit, arms payments and logistics financing so external military assistance shipments accelerate.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_treasury_market_stres</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_treasury_market_stres::short_term_funding_liqui" target="russia_ukraine_war::interceptor_ammo_stock" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater short‑term funding liquidity allows defence contractors and their supply chains to draw working capital, accelerate production and pay for expedited transport, directly increasing the rate at which interceptor munitions are produced and restocked.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_treasury_market_stres</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_treasury_market_stres::short_term_funding_liqui" target="tech_semiconductor_rival::ai_hardware_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A tightening in short‑term funding (higher repo rates or reduced availability) raises bridge‑finance and working‑capital costs for chipmakers, cloud operators and their financiers, prompting firms and investors to delay or scale back near‑term orders and capex for AI hardware.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_treasury_market_stres</data>
  <data key="d39">tech_semiconductor_rival</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_treasury_market_stres::short_term_funding_liqui" target="tech_semiconductor_rival::supply_chain_lead_times" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Reduced short‑term funding availability forces component suppliers and contract manufacturers to cut inventory purchases and production smoothing, producing shipment bottlenecks and lengthening end‑to‑end lead times for AI hardware components.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_treasury_market_stres</data>
  <data key="d39">tech_semiconductor_rival</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_treasury_market_stres::short_term_funding_liqui" target="us_iran_confrontation::trade_rerouting_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter short‑term funding liquidity increases the cost and counterparty risk of dollar settlement, prompting traders and shippers to reroute payments and cargoes via alternative intermediaries and corridors to avoid unreliable/expensive clearing channels.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_treasury_market_stres</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
</edge>
