<edge source="tech_semiconductor_rival::trade_controls_ai" target="russia_ukraine_war::missile_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Stricter export controls that block advanced semiconductors and specialized AI chips to Russian defense contractors reduce the availability of guidance, seeker and flight‑control electronics for cruise/precision missiles, lowering the number of serviceable munitions Russia can produce and launch.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">tech_semiconductor_rival</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="tech_semiconductor_rival::trade_controls_ai" target="us_iran_confrontation::sanctions_enforcement" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">When governments tighten AI export controls they typically fold new licensing requirements and interdiction priorities into existing sanctions apparatuses, prompting more investigations, cross‑border compliance checks and punitive actions against shipments to Iran.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">tech_semiconductor_rival</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="tech_semiconductor_rival::trade_controls_ai" target="us_iran_confrontation::trade_rerouting_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">More restrictive AI export rules make direct legal supply to sanctioned destinations harder, causing exporters and buyers to route consignments through intermediary jurisdictions and transshipment networks to evade controls.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">tech_semiconductor_rival</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="tech_semiconductor_rival::trade_controls_ai" target="us_iran_confrontation::third_party_imports" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">By constraining primary suppliers, stricter AI trade controls increase demand for intermediated purchases and brokered shipments, raising the volume of goods Iran acquires via third‑party commercial actors.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">tech_semiconductor_rival</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_confrontation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="tech_semiconductor_rival::trade_controls_ai" target="us_treasury_market_stres::central_bank_ops" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter export controls on AI components can prompt foreign official and private holders to reduce purchases or rebalance U.S. Treasury holdings, creating dislocations and volatility that trigger expanded Fed/central‑bank repo facilities and temporary market‑backstop operations.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">tech_semiconductor_rival</data>
  <data key="d39">us_treasury_market_stres</data>
</edge>
